\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:Indonesia Shares End Up 0.1%;3550-3600 Band Tipped\b0\par\par\uc2 1,147 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2011\par 10:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0952 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end up 0.1% higher at 3569.144 in moderate volume, off an intraday low of 3518.960, on late bargain-buying by most local institutional funds despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  indicating a likely interest rate hike, traders say; they expect the market to continue to consolidate Monday and tip the main index to move in a 3550-3600 range. "The main index managed to close in positive territory despite selling pressure from foreign funds amid concerns over debt problems in Europe," says a trader Valbury Securities. Among gainers, Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) closed up 1.0% at IDR5,150, rebounding from a IDR4,950 low, BCA (BBCA.JK) ended up 2.5% at IDR6,050, off an intraday low of 5,750, while coal producer Bumi (BUMI.JK) closed up 0.8% at IDR3,175, off its 3,075 low. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0951 GMT [Dow Jones] Despite the strong bounce seen in EUR/JPY Mizuho Corporate bank's Nicole Elliott says all elements of the daily chart suggest a short position. She expects the cross to consolidate under the daily Ichimoku cloud, which comes in around 111.00 and for a strategy would attempt small shorts at market, with a stop above 112.20 for downside targets of 109.00 and possibly 108.50. EUR/JPY now at 110.88. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0948 GMT [Dow Jones] The Hungarian government's amendment proposal to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bill, aimed at changing the rules of appointing Monetary Policy Council rate setters, is a clear move against \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence, \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  says. Notes the proposal, which includes that the Parliament's economic committee should nominate four out of seven rate setters, strips the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor of his right to appoint two MPC members, Danske adds. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0947 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PKR falls to 85.56 in late trade from 85.70 late Thursday. "Import demand has been weak of late, which is causing the dollar to slip whenever exporters come in to cash out some of their earnings," says a dealer. Moreover, he adds, a lack of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the PKR's rise is also dampening U.S. dollar demand. But he expects \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to begin buying dollars soon to protect exporters from the rise in the PKR and tips a 85.60-85.65 range Monday. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0946 GMT [Dow Jones] Non-core euro-zone debt is likely to outperform the German bund market in the short-term, with Italian BTPs favored, says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . The bank notes upcoming 10-year and 15-year supply from Spain, Jan. 20, and a potential 10-year syndicated issue next week from Belgium should limit the spread tightening against bunds of these markets, while Italy is not expected to issue longer-dated debt until Jan. 28 when EUR4 billion of 10-year supply is inked in. However, Credit Agricole says if the improved sentiment in the peripheral markets continues Spanish 10-year paper has already priced in an early concession ahead of next week's auction, and suggests going long the Spanish/Italian 10-year spread. 10-year bunds currently yield 3.05%, unchanged from Thursday. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0946 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty, along with the ILS, CZK and RUB have room to strengthen, says \uc2 UBS\uc2 , which sees the EUR/PLN at 3.60 at the end of 2011. In terms of economic performance, \uc2 UBS\uc2  places Poland in the same category as Turkey, Israel, Egypt and Nigeria -- countries that are in "decent shape" with output gaps narrowing and inflation pressure perhaps building up soon. The bank sees Poland's GDP rising 3.6% in 2010, 3.9% in 2011, and 3.9% again in 2012%. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0944 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts fell to session lows after UK factory gate inflation data but are now back to the levels before the release. The data show output prices rose at an annual 4.2% rate in December vs forecasts of a 3.9% rise. March gilts now down 0.24 at 117.40 vs 117.30 session low. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0944 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is steady at 9,065 in thin volume as the market lack fresh leads, dealers say. "We still expects the rupiah to strengthen on inflows and strong fundamentals, it's just a matter of time and of course, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (suspected) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer at local bank says, tipping the pair to stay in a 9,030-9,070 range next week. BI's Gov. Darmin Nasution says the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will let the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate gradually. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0940 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds have pared gains while gilts are now in negative territory, with yield spreads on peripheral euro-zone government bonds narrowing further. In addition, French Finance Minister Christine Lagarde says officials are looking at raising the size of the EFSF, which could feed into concerns about an increase in German costs of bailing out its neighbours. March bunds are now unchanged at 124.64, and March gilts are down 0.24 at 117.40. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0939 GMT [Dow Jones] The euro's across-the-board surge has broken many short-term resistance levels notes \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . However, the bank says with the exception of EUR/CHF, where the risk is toward 1.31 and possibly 1.34, there is little evidence that the current move will be a long-term game changer. EUR/CHF now at 1.2894. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0939 GMT [Dow Jones] HUF weakens slightly, correcting from a recent peak on increased risk appetite, in turn the result of favorable bond auction results both in euro zone periphery countries and the region in recent days. EUR/HUF is 275.25 from 274.75 late Thursday. Takarekbank sees the EUR/HUF cross stable around 275. Forecasts a downward correction in EUR/USD later today, therefore doesn't expect significant HUF strengthening. \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says 275 is a significant resistance level in EUR/HUF, which is unlikely to be broken in the absence of market-moving news or announcement.(veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0935 GMT [Dow Jones] Despite the slight rise in the Swiss December import and producer price index, the underlying inflation pressure remains very subdued, says \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 . "Apart from energy, metals and agricultural products, nearly all other goods prices declined in December, partly reflecting the impact of the franc's appreciation," according to economist Fabian Heller. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com) [ 01-14-11 0452ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110114e71e0006m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
