\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah stabilises; Taiwan dollar climbs\b0\par\par\uc2 774 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2011\par 04:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah stabilises on foreign fund inflows-trader\par \par \uc2 * Taiwan dollar hits 13-yr high\par \par \uc2 * Thai baht supported ahead of rate decision\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah was little changed versus the dollar on Wednesday, stabilising after a recent sell-off, and the Taiwan dollar hit a 13-year high, with both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported by foreign fund inflows.\par \par \uc2 Traders said dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped lend support to the rupiah, which has come under pressure this month as investors booked profits after a strong rally last year.\par \par \uc2 Foreign players were active sellers of the dollar against the rupiah in the spot market, said a trader for a European bank in Indonesia.\par \par \uc2 "Looks like some fresh inflows," the trader said, adding that offshore funds and real money investors seemed to be buying the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar rose on the back of foreign fund inflows into the equity market, while the Thai baht rose ahead of a rate decision by its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar hit a 13-year high against the dollar, as more foreign money flew into the stock market.\par \par \uc2 George Chou, deputy governor of Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters exporters should hedge against a Taiwan dollar appreciation, indicating the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may rise further.\par \par \uc2 "If the stock market keeps rising, the Taiwan dollar may go past T$29," said one trader at a local bank.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar hit a 13-year high T$29.056 to the dollar. After trimming some gains, the Taiwan dollar stood at T$29.100 compared to Tuesday's close of T$29.700.\par \par \uc2 INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars against the rupiah early on Wednesday, and the dollar's broad weakness also lent support to the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 An equities rally helped to buoy the rupiah, with Indonesian shares surging 2.3 percent , rebounding from a three-month low struck the previous day.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was little changed against the rupiah at 9,045 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar edged up 0.4 percent against the rupiah in January as investors covered their short dollar positions to book profits in the wake of the dollar's 4.4 percent slide against the rupiah last year.\par \par \uc2 THAI BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht rose against the dollar, supported by market expectations of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raising interest rates later on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar came under good selling pressure against the baht right away, in line with broad-based dollar-selling overseas. Macro funds were cited selling the dollar against the baht, with dollar selling interest seen both on- and offshore.\par \par \uc2 Most analysts polled by Reuters expect the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  to raise interest rates by 25 basis points to 2.25 percent at its policy decision due at 0730 GMT, with a few forecasting that rates will be held steady. [ID:nSGE70B00M]\par \par \uc2 But some market players are expecting a hike of 50 basis points on food inflation worries, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Change on the day at   0646 GMT                      \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move