\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:Indonesia Bonds Down;Tipped To Extend Fall Next Wk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2011\par 11:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1012 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia local government bonds continue to fall on a broad sell-off amid high inflation pressures, traders say. Two traders at a local securities firms say the falls may continue well into the middle of next week before selective bargain-hunting by investors emerges. The five-year yield is up at 6.78% from 6.69% Thursday, the 10-year yield is higher at 7.79% from 7.70%, the 15-year yield is at 8.40% from 8.32%, and the 20-year yield is at 9.17% compared with 9.04%. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1011 GMT [Dow Jones] CZK trades lower at 24.657-24.677 against the euro from 24.592 late Thursday as investors are closing short positions following a string of impressive Czech data releases this week, says a trader at Raiffeisenbank in Prague. "The good news is out and they can close positions; it's typical profit taking," the trader says. "In one month we could be lower, testing the 24.50 psychological level if German and Czech industry go well." (sean.carney@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1007 GMT [Dow Jones] The Markit iTraxx corporate credit indexes are still little moved on the day as banks and sovereigns continue to suffer, says data-provider Markit. Notes both the Europe and Crossover indexes are nearly flat at 108/109bps and 429/433bps, respectively, with trading light ahead of key U.S. labor data due at 1330 GMT. However, says banks are wider after the European Commission's proposed framework for senior bank debt, and sovereigns are continuing to move out amid worries about impending government bond supply. Markit SovX Western Europe index is 5bps wider at 216/218bps. (art.patnaude@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1005 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end down 1.4% at 1036.45, snapping three straight sessions of gains in active trade. Most big caps retreat on consolidation mode. The SET Index is expected to continue to consolidate next week as the downside is weighed by expectations the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hike its benchmark rate Wednesday, says Asia Plus Securities' Therdsak Thaveethiratham. He adds, the selling force in certain tax benefit mutual funds due to be redeemed is likely to continue. He tips support at 1030 and resistance at 1050. Among the most active stocks, \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) is down 2.8% at THB102.50, \uc2 True Corp\uc2 . (TRUE.TH) slides 8.7% to THB6.30, PTT (PTT.TH) falls 3.0% to THB322 and Thai Oil (TOP.TH) drops 3.3% at THB73.25. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1004 GMT [Dow Jones] Takarekbank expects Hungary's industrial output to have accelerated further in December after unexpectedly strong November growth data, released Friday. Adjusted November output is up 4.3% on the month and 14.5% higher on the year. Economist Gergely Suppan says it's likely December growth rose due to demand growth from German car manufacturers and a new tire plant owned by Hankook that began production at the end of November. Suppan expects strong industrial data to support Hungarian financial market assets given the implied improvement in economic prospects. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1001 GMT [Dow Jones] The impact of the severe floods in Queensland is being felt beyond Australia's borders and the AUD, notes \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . The bank says alternative suppliers of the affected commodities will benefit in terms of increased demand and higher prices and this is another reason to be short AUD/CAD, in addition to China's continued policy tightening. AUD/CAD now trades at 0.9923. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1000 GMT [Dow Jones] Norway's manufacturing output for November comes in at +0.9% on the month, reversing the previous month's dip, and the rise was higher than expected, says Handelsbanken. "If the December reading stays flat, the 4Q annualised growth in manufacturing production will be 3.1%, not much above \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2 's forecast," notes Handelsbanken, so this "shouldn't significantly alter \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2 's view of the manufacturing sector." (charles.duxbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0944 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end down 2.8% at 3631.453 in moderate volume as foreign funds trim their positions due to growing concern over the country's inflation. Investors are worried because rising food prices will add to Indonesia's inflationary pressures in January, traders say; they add, higher inflation could inspire the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike policy rate next month. Traders tip the main index to trade in a 3600-3670 range Monday. "Selling in most interest rate-sensitive and commodity stocks drove the main index lower despite sporadic bargain-buying by local funds," says a trader with Erdhika Securities. Among decliners: carmaker Astra (ASII.JK) is down 3.9% at IDR49,000, \uc2 Bank Mandiri\uc2  (BMRI.JK) is down 4.5% at IDR6,400, while Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) is down 5.3% at IDR9,800. Foreigners are net sellers of IDR1.5 trillion worth of shares. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0943 GMT [Dow Jones] The Sensex is down 2.2% at 19,750.33 on growing concerns India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon raise interest rates to tackle rising food inflation, say local dealers. Investors are deeply worried that "the RBI may raise policy rates by 50 bps (basis points) after market hours today and that is causing the sell-off," says a senior dealer. The RBI's next policy review is scheduled for January 25 but investors fear the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will move early to combat high food inflation, the dealers say. Among losers, \uc2 Infosys Technologies\uc2  (500209.BY) is down 2.8% at INR3,382.00, \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) is 2.1% lower at INR1,061 and \uc2 Housing Development Finance Corp\uc2 .(500010.BY) is 3.0% lower at INR685.35. The Sensex is likely to find support at 19,680, according to Dow Jones technical analysis(sudeep.jain@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0934 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is higher at 9,020 from 8,993 late Thursday, breaching the 9,000 resistance level, tracking the dollar's gains against several Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and as foreigners continue to cash in their gains from local stock and bond markets, traders say. "We don't see Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  today. They may see the rupiah slide as roughly in line with the region's," says a trader with a foreign bank, tipping the pair to trade in a 8,980-9,040 range next week. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0932 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds are higher in lackluster trade. Prices rebound after their recent sharp fall, tracking gains late Thursday in U.S. Treasurys. "There's still some demand in the medium-term bonds. Overall, the emerging market remains attractive for investors," says a local dealer. He adds, the focus is on the U.S. non-farm payroll data later in the day and the message from the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  after its rate decision next week. The market expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike its policy rate by 25 bps Wednesday. The bid/offer yields of issues due December 2015 are quoted at 3.16%/3.14% from 3.20%/3.18% late Thursday, while October 2017 yields are quoted at 3.44%/3.37% from 3.52%/3.42% and June 2019 yields are at 3.52%/3.45% from 3.65%/3.55%. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0931 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CHF turns lower as expected, the down trend of the last two months is intact and the Fibonacci extension target of 1.2150 is alive and well, says \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . Now at 1.2520; the bank says support at 1.24 may hold for a temporary bounce. However, any break below opens risk to the aforementioned target. (gary.stride@dowjones.com) [ 01-07-11 0512ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110107e7170005v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
