\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Falls Below 9,000; 8,970-9,000 Tipped Fri\b0\par\par\uc2 1,242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2010\par 11:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1021 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is lower at 8,983 from 9,005 late Wednesday amid the USD's slide against its major rivals amid quiet trade with many players on holidays, dealers say. Two dealers say they also suspect Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the 8,980 level to slow the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's appreciation. A dealer at a local bank tips the pair to trade in a 8,970-9,000 band Friday. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1017 GMT [Dow Jones] In Thursday's Money Talks column, Alen Mattich picks his top economics blogs. (alen.mattich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1005 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR forward premia reverse early losses to trade a tad higher as hawkish comments from a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official stoke the growing talk of a rate hike at the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary policy meeting in late January, says a trader with a privately-run bank. The one-year forward premium is at 2.54 from 2.53 late Wednesday. "Earlier in the session premia had actually come down in line with the spot, indicating selling interest from exporters," the trader says. But the flow wasn't strong enough to blunt a wave of paying after the RBI deputy governor KC Chakrabarty said the recent pause in rates at the last \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting in December doesn't mean more rate hikes are off the table. The remarks assume importance after another uptick in the latest weekly food price index reading.(bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1002 GMT [Dow Jones] parallel strength of JPY and AUD is unusual says Lena Komileva, head of G7 Market Economics at Tullett Prebon. However, instead of being a 'risk-off,' or commodity trade, Komileva says the current moves are instead a reflection of a universal bias toward dollar weakness. Earlier Thursday AUD/USD hit a post-flotation high of 1.0197 while USD/JPY printed a fresh 7-week low of 81.28. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1000 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds extend losses in afternoon trade on RBI Deputy Governor's indication the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's temporary pause stance doesn't mean a halt to rate hikes, says a state-run bank trader. The comments add to concern inflation may force the RBI to hike rates again in January as the latest food price index data Thursday registered another uptick, he says. "Also, the finance minister expects inflation by March around 6.5%, which is higher than the RBI comfort level. Every bit of news today is weighing on bond prices," the trader says. The most-traded 8.08% 2022 bond is at 100.10, off the intraday high of 100.31 and compared with 100.26 last close. He tips the 8.08% 2022 bond yield in a 8.03%-8.08% band, with the current yield at 8.06%. (sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0951 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end the last trading day of the year down 0.2% at 1032.76 in light volume; but the index has gained 41% in 2010. "I think for the first week of 2011 it will be slow again, but after that I think we'll see some funds flowing back. Also, I think sentiment towards equities should be quite positive, here and globally," says \uc2 Kim Eng Securities\uc2  strategist Mayuree Chowvikran. She tips the market to trade in a 1020-1040 range next week. The market will be closed Friday and Monday. Among top actives, \uc2 True Corp\uc2  (TRUE.TH) down 1.4% at THB7.10, \uc2 Charoen Pokphand Foods\uc2  (CPF.TH) down 0.4% at THB24.70, \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) down 1.4% at THB103.50, PTT Chemical (PTTCH.TH) down 1.3% at THB147, IRPC (IRPC.TH) +4% at THB6.50, Thai Oil (TOP.TH) +0.6% at THB78.25. (leigh.murray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0950 GMT [Dow Jones] 10-year Treasurys are down slightly in low volumes in London after a rally Wednesday following the successful 7-year auction. 10-year Treasurys yield is at 3.366%, up 0.016 percentage points. "Most of the business we've seen is month-end and year-end house-keeping for real money investors," one market participant says. The data schedule Thursday has weekly jobless claims at 1330 GMT. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0945 GMT [Dow Jones] China onshore IRS are higher after the PBOC's 3-month bill yield rose 20 bps to 2.0156%. The 1-year IRS is up 3 bps at 3.14%-3.23%, The 5-year is up 1 bp at 3.80%-3.89%. But a trader at a Shanghai-based local bank says rate hike expectations for next year are priced in. "We forecast there will be 2 or 3 rate hikes in 2011 and the swaps already reflect 4 to 5 rate hikes," she adds. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0939 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds are mixed in sluggish trade; volume is razor-thin as most participants have already taken off for new year holidays. "We see some firm bids from certain offshore players in five- to 10-year bonds" but yields are still rangebound, says trader. Yields are expected to rise next week as investors fret about possible BOT rate hike on January 12. The bid/offer yields of issues due December 2015 are quoted at 3.24%/3.20% vs 3.25%/3.20% late Wednesday, while October 2017 yields are steady at 3.50%/3.45% and June 2019 yields are at 3.61%/3.56% vs 3.62%/3.53%. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0939 GMT [Dow Jones] The usual month-end demand is lifting EUR/GBP, says a UK bank trader. The cross now trades at the day's high of 0.8555. \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  pegs next resistance at 0.8596, ahead of 0.8645. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0929 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY printed a fresh 7-week low of 81.28 in Asia Thursday with exporter sales and lower US yields seemingly the main drivers. The spot now trades at 81.47, nearest support comes in at 81.22 and 81.00 says \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 . (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0928 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end up 0.1% at 3703.512 in light volume, led by foreign buying in select blue chips on hopes for strong 4Q earnings, traders say. The main index is up 46% since the start of the year. Traders expect profit-taking may occur Monday amid concerns of higher inflation for December, with data due to be announced Monday. They tip the index to bottom at 3650. "Some investors prefer to take cash ahead of the year-end holiday," says a trader with First Asia Capital. Foreigners are net buyers of IDR222 billion worth of shares. Indonesia's market is closed Friday for holiday. Among gainers, carmaker Astra (ASII.JK) is up 1.0% at IDR54,550, \uc2 Indosat\uc2  (ISAT.JK) is up 4.9% at IDR5,400 and gas and oil company Medco (MEDC.JK) is up 6.3% at IDR3,375. Profit taking hits Bank Danamon (BDMN.JK), which is down 1.7% at IDR5,700. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com) [ 12-30-10 0521ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101230e6cu0005g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
