\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:Bank Indonesia Drops 3-Mo SBI;Curb Hot Money -OCBC\b0\par\par\uc2 1,349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2010\par 10:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0910 GMT [Dow Jones] Bank Indonesia's move to drop 3-month certificates, or SBI, in today's auction signifies \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's concerns on speculative flows, may extend minimum holding period of SBIs, says OCBC; move "is a bid to continue pushing investors to go into the longer-end papers, which in turn is meant to reduce speculative flows in the market." Adds, concerns on sudden outflows remain; "we would not be surprised if they were to implement a longer minimum holding period for SBI bills to 3 months from 1 month" currently. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0908 GMT [Dow Jones] Nomura still reckons GBP will outperform but prefers to remove the directional USD bias inherent in the short EUR/GBP trade it entered on November 2. It argues that EUR/GBP tends to be positively correlated with EUR/USD, so a renewed USD sell-off could hurt the trade. As a result, it is switching to a GBP basket trade, with two thirds invested against EUR and one third against USD. The EUR/GBP trade is closed for a profit of around 1.3% of the amount invested. "We enter this new basket trade at 0.8620 EUR/GBP and 1.5990 GBP/USD. We will run a 1.0% basket stop loss... We allocate $10m within our $100m model portfolio," Nomura says. (martin.essex@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0907 GMT [Dow Jones] As tensions rise ahead of the G-20 summit starting this Thursday in Seoul, expect the USD to benefit, says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . The bank notes that the whole issue of QEII, which had initially hit the USD, has now been pushed onto the back burner, while news of China's even larger than expected trade surplus will fuel discontent. "The USD often benefits if there is tension on the international scene. As a result EUR/USD might ease further initially," the bank says. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0905 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: China's October industrial production likely +13.4% on-year vs September's +13.3%, according to Dow Jones poll of 12 economists. Survey also shows urban fixed asset investment likely +24.4% in January-October period on-year vs January-September's +24.5%. Survey shows China's industrial output, investment remain relatively stable, despite cooling measures this year such as first ever rate hike in almost three years in October, continuous measures to cool property market. "Industry seems to have achieved a soft landing, but with industrial output growth slightly weaker than during the pre-crisis period," says Capital Economics economist Mark Williams. Data due Thursday. (li.liu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0901 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia's real GDP growth likely slowed to 5.6% on-year in 3Q vs +8.9% in 2Q, +10.1% in 1Q says RHB Research; 3Q industrial production growth slows to +4.3% on-year vs +11.1% in 2Q. "Going forward, we expect the global economy to expand at a more moderate pace in 2011," says RHB. Adds, in tandem with slowdown in global demand, country's exports may also slow in 2011 but domestic demand growth may stay resilient but grow at more moderate pace of 5.5% in 2011 vs +5.9% tipped for 2010. House expects real GDP growth to slow to 5.0% in 2011 from +7.3% forecast for 2010. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0856 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR lower at 8,895 vs 8,904 late yesterday in line with USD's weakness vs regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers say; no sign of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent pair from sliding below 8,900, two dealers say. "I was surprised that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't seem to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one of them says; adds pair may slide further tomorrow, but profit taking evident in local bond market today could limit USD/IDR slide to 8,885; 8,910 resistance tipped. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0855 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 UBS\uc2  downgrades Sandvik (SAND.SK) to sell from neutral. "We believe the stock should derate going forward with 4Q results or news suggesting weaker commodity prices being potential catalysts for a de-rating," the bank says. Adds that of SKF (SKF-B.SK), Sandvik and Atlas Copco (ATCO-A.SK) it still prefers SKF and thinks it deserves to outperform relative to the other two. Keeps SEK95 target unchanged due to better cash flow offsetting EPS downgrades. Shares -1.9% at SEK111.50. (sven.grundberg@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0853 GMT [Dow Jones] The December 10-year gilt opened below the 123.81 support level and "a settlement below here will be a further negative, suggesting the directional risk is beginning to skew to the downside once more and that a deeper sell-off is on the cards," says Richard Adcock, \uc2 UBS\uc2  technical strategist. "The bearish themes are backed up by the momentum/trending relationship, with the MACD still below its zero line, and we will now look for a closing cross lower in stochastics over the next few days to confirm the resumption of the downside that can test the more important longer term support at 121.93/122.22." Support lies at 123.20, 122.22 and 121.93. (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0849 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex trapped in narrow band, now flat at 20,915.29 on absence of fresh triggers, subdued cues from Asian peers. "Most of the major company results are already out and there are no major events to look forward to," says Prakash Diwan of Networth Stock-Broking. Another analyst tips index in 20,500-21,200 band near-term. Among actives, \uc2 Tata Motors\uc2  (500570.BY) +3.3% at INR1312 as 2Q net profit surged to INR22.23 billion, up vs INR217.8 million year earlier. However, \uc2 Hindalco Industries\uc2  (500440.BY), which posted lower-than-expected 2Q net profit late Tuesday, down 3.6% at INR223.45 and Cipla (500087.BY) down 1.7% at INR343.70. (swagata.gupta@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0846 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia's wider balance of payments data is likely positive for IDR and local bond market, analysts say. Indonesia's BOP stood at $6.96 billion in 3Q vs $5.42 billion in 2Q; contributed by $6.48 billion of capital and financial account (vs $4.37 billion in 2Q), $1.31 billion of current account (vs $1.8 billion in 2Q). "The erosion of the current account surplus is happening at a gradual pace...For the near future, portfolio inflows may continue to be rapid especially in the wake of the Fed's QE2," Bank Danamon's Helmi Arman says. ING shares similar view, but warns not getting too excited until inflation subsides. "We will turn bullish on government bonds after the threat of an above-6.0% inflation print has passed." (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0842 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty is higher as foreign investors are moving into Poland with its relatively high interest rates, a trader says. Adds the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to test EUR/PLN3.8850 level, vital resistance toward further strengthening in anticipation of rate hikes. EUR/PLN is at 3.8901 from 3.9017, USD/PLN at 2.8190 from 2.8398. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones]USD/INR implied volatilities lower on moribund spot, but finding support at current levels from reviving concerns on health of global economy, says trader with foreign bank; 1-month ATMF at 7.50%/8.25% vs 7.75%/8.50% late Tuesday. Also, approaching G-20 meet also adding to demand for protection from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings, bolstering front-end of curve, says trader. Adds, some interest on 3-month to 1-year vega neutral spreads, likely to cover gap in risk bucket rather than play on view for curve. (bijou.george@dowjones.com) [ 11-10-10 0410ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101110e6ba00060\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
