\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Lower; 8,920-8,930 Band Tipped Thursday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2010\par 10:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0933 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR tad lower late at 8,922 vs 8,925 yesterday in thin volume amid lack of fresh leads; dealer say; tips 8,920-8,930 band Thursday. "The market wants to hear Bank Indonesia's message tomorrow, especially on the liquidity issue, as the BI rate will most likely be unchanged," dealer at local bank says. A senior dealer at foreign bank says "I personally don't see any major impact if the Fed announce QE2 tonight, as it's well priced in. Moreover, BI will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and provide support for the pair." Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will hold rate policy meeting tommorow, market expects the bank to stay pat. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0932 GMT [Dow Jones]Sweden's political party leaders will today hold their first debate since the country's general election and the breakdown of the center-left "Red-Green" alliance, SEB bank highlights. The leaders may give signals about their willingness to work together in the new parliament and on which questions, says the bank. Sweden's two-year bond yield trades flat at 1.380 while the 10-year trades 0.5bp lower at 2.765. (charles.duxbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0927 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex holds early gains, last +0.7% at 20,495.17 on positive global equities, buying in select large caps stocks. 22 of the 30 index issues trade higher; with metals leading rise, while \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) down 0.7% at INR1,066.50 on profit-taking for 2nd straight session. "There is selective buying by funds on the back of cash refunds from \uc2 Coal India\uc2  IPO due to high subscriptions," hopes of more money flowing into market from expected announcement of possible quantitative easing measures from Fed later in the global day, says dealer at domestic brokerage. Adds volume on BSE cash market at about INR38.21 billion, lower than last session as most participants await Fed outcome. Expects Sensex in 20,400-20,800 range near term. \uc2 Tata Steel\uc2  (500470.BY) +2.0% at INR610, Sterlite (500900.BY) +3.7% at INR176. SBI (500112.BY) +2.2% at INR3,274, ICICI Bank (532174.BY) +1.2% at INR1,244.90. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] The franc may appreciate versus the euro if the Swiss consumer price index, due Thursday, and unemployment, due Monday, show positive readings, according to BayernLB. "If Swiss inflation rises clearly above zero, and unemployment continues to fall, this could stir speculation about an earlier increase in interest rates, and buoy the franc," says analyst Frank Armbruster. EUR/CHF at 1.3749 by 0922 GMT. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] The Turkish lira is stronger on increasing appetite for risk in global markets. USD/TRY trades at 1.4099, from 1.4150 Tuesday. Meanwhile bonds are weaker after Turkish October CPI rose 1.83% on the month, above market expectations. The benchmark August 8, 2012 bond trades at 7.65% from 7.58% Tuesday. Analysts forecast TRY will trade between 1.3977 and 1.4482, and the benchmark bond between 7.52% and 7.73%, in the short term.\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end down 0.6% at 3605.673 in moderate volume, but off intraday low of 3590.873, as foreign investors continue to take profit in most blue chips after recent gains, traders say; expect shares to continue to consolidate tomorrow ahead of Bank Indonesia meeting on interest rates; tip index in 3590-3630 range; index still up 42% since start of 2010. "Foreign funds took profit ahead of the Fed's meeting, weighing down overall sentiment here," says trader at Valbury Securities. Foreigners net sellers of IDR178 billion worth of shares vs IDR523 billion net sells yesterday. Among decliners, car maker Astra (ASII.JK) down 1.7% at IDR55,600 on profit taking, heavyweight Telkom (TLKM.JK) down 3.0% at IDR8,050, while \uc2 Indosat\uc2  (ISAT.JK) down 0.8% at IDR5,950 after their ADRs fell in NY. Bucking trend, Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) +0.8% at IDR12,200 on strong 9M10 earnings.(edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0923 GMT [Dow Jones] The complete contrast between the Fed and the RBA will be laid bare tonight says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . While on Tuesday the RBA became the first G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move monetary policy into restrictive territory and talk of "modest tightening" the Fed is highly likely to become even more expansive. The bank says while today's FOMC meeting will be decisive for AUD/USD short-term, the medium-term prospects look good for the rate to trade above parity on a sustainable basis. AUD/USD now at 0.9986. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0920 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/THB lower at 29.745 vs 29.83-29.84 late yesterday in tandem with bearish USD tone. However, suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow THB's rise helps to limit pair's downside, say two dealers. All eyes now on details of expected Fed asset purchase program due later in global day. "The dollar/baht direction in the near-term will be determined by the size of the U.S. liquidity injection. However, the pair is more exposed to the downside as sale orders from exporters look pretty heavy," says one dealer. Support at 29.65, resistance at 29.85. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0920 GMT [Dow Jones] Political pressures in Ireland are adding to the stressed levels of Irish bond yields this week. The 10-year Irish bond yield has risen to 7.394% from Monday's low at 7.02%. "The resignation of Irish government TD McDaid yesterday has lowered the majority of the Irish coalition to just three; this includes two independents. Clearly the ability of the government to pass the budget by the December deadline is on a knife edge," says Jane Foley, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 . "To make matter worse there are rising concerns that the government may have to earmark more money for Allied Irish given the lenders reported difficulties in finding a buyer for its UK business." The 10-year Irish bond yield has risen to 7.395% from Monday's low at 7.02% and 495 bps above German bunds. (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0918 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia shares end 0.1% higher at 1507.60; index caught in tight 4- point range all day as investors shy away from taking aggressive positions ahead of FOMC outcome later in global day. "There was some buying interest in lower liners, but overall people weren't too interested in taking large positions," dealer says. Technology stocks led gains after Unisem's (5005.KU) strong 3Q earnings. Maybank IB says index could re-test all-time high of 1524.69 soon, with plantation stocks likely leading gains given recent underperformance, plus helped by strong crude palm oil prices. Tips immediate resistance at 1509, then 1524; support at 1506, then 1490. Market breadth positive with 503 advancers vs 280 decliners; \uc2 China Ouhua Winery\uc2  (5188.KU) +9.2% at MYR0.655 on debut, Unisem +4.9% at MYR1.92, JCY (5161.KU) +2.5% at MYR1.01; decliners DiGi.Com (6947.KU) down 0.6% at MYR25.40, AirAsia (5099.KU) down 1.2% at MYR2.53. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0918 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty is up, in tandem with the euro. A further strengthening of the zloty as well as other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will depend on the magnitude of the QE2 program the Fed is set to unveil late Wednesday, a dealer says. EUR/PLN is at 3.9381 from 3.9545 late Tuesday; USD/PLN at 2.8053 from 2.8175. Average yield on 2-year bonds is unchanged at 4.75% from late Tuesday, 5-year also unchanged at 5.23%, 10-year at 5.66% from 5.67%. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0915 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds higher with heavy buying by offshore players in late trade; mainly in 5-year tenor papers. "Foreigners' view is biased toward U.S. dollar weakness in the future, no matter what the size of the quantitative easing measures might be," says bond dealer. Investors awaiting details of QE, expected to be announced after FOMC's meeting ends tonight. Dealer tips yields likely to fall by up to 5 bps Thursday. Bid/offer yields of issue due December 2015 quoted at 2.80%/2.77% vs 2.88%/2.85% late yesterday, November 2016 at 2.99%/2.90% vs 3.03/2.98%, June 2019 at 3.10%/3.05% vs 3.12%/3.07%. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com) [ 11-03-10 0533ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101103e6b300059\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
