\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Indonesia Shares Likely Higher; 3630 Resistance\b0\par\par\uc2 1,320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2010\par 04:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0211 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares likely tad higher, tracking gains in several Asian markets like Japan, China, Singapore, traders say; tip index in 3680-3630 range after shares Friday end down 0.6% at 3597.031. "I think, overall, the market may continue to consolidate amid an absence of fresh leads from the domestic economic front," says trader at First Asia Capital. Bellwether Telkom (TLKM.JK) may rise on bargain buying after falling more than 4% last week, while car maker Astra (ASII.JK) may drop on profit-taking. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com) ()\f28 \par \par \uc2 0209 GMT [Dow Jones] Gold down 0.7%, silver down 2% as more profit taking kicks in after weak close Friday and dollar strength in early Asia trade; EUR/USD breaks through 1.4000 support (last at 1.3907) after dovish comments from ECB Trichet over weekend. "Gold's lackluster performance on Friday may fuel more profit-taking as investors fear that the gold rally may take a breather after the recent meteoric rise in prices," says Phillip Futures. Spot gold at $1,359.60/oz, down $9.30 since Friday's NY close while spot silver at $23.85/oz, down 47 cents. (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0200 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY opens higher after U.S. Treasury delays \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report, in which China could be named \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator. USD/CNY at 6.6502 vs Friday's close of 6.6412, expected to consolidate below central parity rate of 6.6541. "The dollar is expected to fall this week on hot money inflows and strong yuan demand at the end of the month," says Guangzhou-based foreign bank trader; it's common practice for exporters to sell USD at month's end to banks on request of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (jean.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0157 GMT [Dow Jones] IMM commitment of traders report shows net JPY-long (vs USD) non-commercial positions fell slightly to 48,285 contracts in week to Oct. 12 vs 49,206 contracts in week earlier, suggesting speculators unwilling to increase bets on further JPY strength as they see chances of another round of MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasing. "The yen-long positions have been piled up to a significantly high level," says Osamu Takashima, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank Japan. Expects \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  players to start taking profit on long-JPY positions in near term. (Kosaku.Narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0156 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan government bonds mostly lower, weighed by profit taking, says local bank trader. 5-year yield last at 0.8793% vs 0.8755% Friday, eyed in 0.8700%-0.9000% band for day. 20-year yield last at 1.6915%, steady vs Friday's close, but trader expects 20-year bond biased down in near term. "There are few insurers buying at lows so far today, which could prompt more selling from brokerage houses." Tips 20-year yield in 1.6800%-1.7100% band for day. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0155 GMT [Dow Jones] October HSI futures down 0.2% at 23,693, indicating HSI may only open modestly lower, continuing modest pullback Friday (down 0.4%). Contract ended Friday at 19-point discount to cash, suggests players expecting near-term profit-taking, which unsurprising given HSI rose for 7th straight week, with cumulative gains of 15.3%. October open interest little changed at 112,944 lots. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0150 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR edges up slightly at 8,925 vs 8,920 as local players take profit after Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's supected active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently, showing its resolve not to let greenback fall below 8,920. But, so far this morning \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't heard buying pair as yet. Pair tipped in 8,920-8,930 range for session. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0149 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD tad lower at 30.750 vs 30.793 Friday, but off early low of 30.670 due to Taiex's 1.0% fall, importers buying, says foreign bank trader. "The pair has rarely gone below 31.000 over the past 10 years," so current price attractive to investors, she says. Adds, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step in to slow pair's rise later; as it was suspected of doing so recently. Tips pair in 30.700-30.800 band for day. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0144 GMT [Dow Jones] HK blue chips' pre-open showing HSI's correction may be 1-day thing, after index ended Friday down 0.4%. Gainers outnumber losers at pre-open; those bid up at least 2% include Swire Pacific (0019.HK), \uc2 Hang Lung Properties\uc2  (0101.HK), Sinopec (0019.HK), Shenhua (1088.HK), China Coal (1898.HK); while \uc2 HSBC\uc2  (0005.HK) lone blue chip quoted more than 1% lower. HKEx (0388.HK) indicated flat at HK$180.00 pre-market, while stock very overbought after 47.7% surge since September, any pullback unlikely significant given robust HK market volume. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0141 GMT [Dow Jones] KLCI little changed at 1490.40, supported by gains in plantation stocks. Broader market mixed, with advancers, decliners evenly matched. 2011 budget unveiled by PM Najib Friday failing to make any impression among investors. "Broadly speaking, we see little instantaneous impact from Budget 2011 on our domestic stock exchange as the government's master plan to overhaul the Malaysian economy...may only begin to bear fruit in the medium to longer term," HwangDBS Vickers Research says; pegs immediate resistance at 1495, support at 1465. Among gainers, plantation stocks extend gains amid strong palm oil prices, with Batu Kawan (1899.KU) +7.2% at MYR15.80, Genting Plantations (2291.KU) +0.4% at MYR8.40; among decliners, PLUS (5052.KU) down 0.9% at MYR4.42 as some analysts deem UEM, EPF's MYR23 billion takeover offer unattractive. (benjamin.low@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0140 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares likely higher, expected to test 1000 as fund inflows continue. If benchmark index rises above that psychological level, it may even extend gains to 1020 technical resistance, says Globlex Securities' Head of Equity Investment Strategy Chakkrit Charoenmethachai. "As the dollar remains bearish, it's likely that the fund relocation to the Asian markets would continue," he says. Expects energy, financial plays to lead advance, though gains likely limited on profit-taking; investors think \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  may hold its benchmark rate unchanged at 1.75% at Wednesday policy meeting. Support put at 987. SET Index ended +0.4% at 997.15 Friday. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0133 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore shares slightly higher; STI +0.3% at 3215.13, off 3197 early low, with gainers beating losers 1.7 to 1. Muted gains reflect caution ahead; "(STI) upside is probably limited after the good run we've seen and the market is starting to look a bit tired. The main question is 'did we do enough to warrant the spike above 3200?' I think that question will be answered during the earnings season," says analyst at local brokerage. GLP (MC0.SG) opens at S$2.16 on debut, +10% vs IPO price of S$1.96, gains largely expected after offer 12X subscribed; stock tops volume list. SGX (S68.SG) down 0.8% at S$10.04 after 1QFY11 net profit falls 21% on-year, hurt by lower securities revenue; down 17.1% on-year. China New Town Development (DN4.SG) +5.8%, second most traded stock, on news dual listing in Hong Kong by way of introduction to commence trading October 22. STI resistance tipped at May 2008 peak of 3,267, support at 3,142 last week's low. 271.5 million shares traded so far. (matthew.allen@dowjones.com) [ 10-17-10 2211ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101018e6ai0001d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
