\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Steady; 8,920-8,930 Tipped Monday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,172 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 10:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR unchanged at 8,920, well supported by suspected Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by buying around $50 million at the level, three dealers say. "Capital inflows continue and the dollar is still under selling pressure," one of them says. 8,920-8,930 tipped for Monday, with pair likely to skirt around lower end of range mostly. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0819 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar is on the slide again after enjoying a brief respite overnight. The markets attention is firmly fixed on Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke's speech on monetary policy, which he delivers just before the release of U.S. inflation and retail sales numbers. The euro is trading at the day's high of $1.4114, the pound is up at $1.6053, and the dollar is down at Y81.19. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0813 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD meets with good buying demand below 1.4080 which is hard to cover says a UK bank trader. The spot now trades at 1.4092, just off the day's 1.4098 high. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0805 GMT [Dow Jones] Pakistan shares higher, with fertilizer, oil stocks leading gains; benchmark KSE-100 index +0.3% at 10,447.32. "Foreign investment is the buzz word these days and has convinced local investors to participate in a big way", says dealer. Net foreign investment year-to-date estimated at $411 million, according to National Clearing Co. Adds, "upcoming financial results will also help boost interest in oil, fertilizer and gas companies. However, key concerns for the market is rising inflation as it would press \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to revisit the monetary policy schedule due next month." In September, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised benchmark interest rate by 50 bps to 13.5%. Oil & Gas Development (OGDC.KA) +0.8% at PKR151.20, \uc2 Engro Corp\uc2 . (ENGRO.KA) +0.2% at PKR179.34. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0804 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia's subsidies to various sectors from gasoline to foods likely to rise 22.5% to MYR24.9 billion in 2010 from MYR20.3 billion year earlier, despite recent cuts in subsidies in fuel, sugar, the government says in economic report. "Total subsidy outlay is increasing and is unsustainable," it says, adding recent IMF study finds subsidies "not well-targeted." Of 2010 total, fuel subsidies likely +61.6% on year at MYR10.0 billion due to rising oil prices; assistance for education likely at MYR7.1 billion; other welfare assistance at MYR2.3 billion. Subsidies for interest rate differential, electricity likely MYR1.5 billion, paddy, rice, sugar and flour subsidies total MYR2.3 billion. Subsidies rank as second largest component in government's 2010 operating expenditure. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0801 GMT [Dow Jones] iTraxx Japan Series 14 traded at 104, 105 bps vs yesterday's close of 101 bps, led by widening in consumer lenders' CDS spreads, says dealer at major Japan bank. Credit protection on Acom (8572.TO) done at 600, 605, 610, 720 bps vs yesterday's 520, 540, 550 bps, Acom's 3-year protection at 850 bps. Says index may widen to 110 bps next week as concerns over consumer lending industry expected to persist. Says market participants "focused on whether (such concerns) will affect the entire market's sentiment." Other single-name CDS deals include Japanese USD-denominated sovereign CDS at 54 bps vs 55 bps on Oct. 8, \uc2 NTT DoCoMo\uc2  (9437.TO) at 30 bps vs 27.5 bps on March 10, \uc2 NTT Corp\uc2 . (9432.TO) at 30 bps, unchanged from Feb. 5. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0800 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia forecasts fiscal deficit of 5.4% of GDP in 2011 Vs 5.6% fiscal deficit tipped for 2010, despite 2.8% increase in overall expenditure to MYR212 billion, the government says Friday in annual report on economy. Federal government's revenue projected to rise to MYR165.83 billion in 2011, +2.3% vs estimated MYR162.13 billion in 2010, supported by higher tax revenue from stronger expansion in domestic economic activity. Operating expenditure forecast to expand 7.0% to MYR162.8 billion, in-line with commitments under 10th Malaysia Plan (a five-year infrastructure blueprint that runs from 2011 to 2015) and initiatives under economic transformation plan. (elffie.chew@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0800 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia forecasts fiscal deficit of 5.4% of GDP in 2011 Vs 5.6% fiscal deficit tipped for 2010, despite 2.8% increase in overall expenditure to MYR212 billion, the government says Friday in annual report on economy. Federal government's revenue projected to rise to MYR165.83 billion in 2011, +2.3% vs estimated MYR162.13 billion in 2010, supported by higher tax revenue from stronger expansion in domestic economic activity. Operating expenditure forecast to expand 7.0% to MYR162.8 billion, in-line with commitments under 10th Malaysia Plan (a five-year infrastructure blueprint that runs from 2011 to 2015) and initiatives under economic transformation plan. (elffie.chew@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0757 GMT [Dow Jones] Fed chairman Bernanke speaks on monetary policy this afternoon, but he will avoid direct discussion on the value of the dollar says \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 's Jane Foley, as it is the US Treasury, rather than the Fed that governs dollar policy. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0752 GMT [Dow Jones] There is no sign of a reversal in GBP/USD and that will remain the case while it trades above the 1.5750 area says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2 . The bank favors buying dips looking for a move toward 1.62 and 1.63 fairly soon. GBP/USD now at 1.6036. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0748 GMT [Dow Jones] CHF is likely to trade a neutral tone in the coming week as the strong economy is offset by concern low inflation could prompt \uc2 Swiss National Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 . "On one hand, strong economic fundamentals, including robust domestic demand, low unemployment, and strong PMI readings, are CHF supportive," say analysts Calvin Tse and Tim Davis. "However, low CPI prints may prompt the SNB to reenter the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, especially as other governments across the globe are actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken their own respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it argues. EUR/CHF at 1.3437 and USD/CHF at 0.9543. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0748 GMT [Dow Jones] AUD/USD is looking a little top heavy Friday after Thursday's run toward parity ended in failure. The spot fell to 0.9890 in Asia Friday, matching Thursday's low point, and well of its record high of 0.9996 seen the same day. AUD/USD now trades at 0.9942, with support likely to come in between 0.99 and 0.9880, but with risk of stops below the latter. (gary.stride@dowjones.com) [ 10-15-10 0441ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101015e6af0005k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
