\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Indonesia Shares End +0.2%; 3600-3640 Tipped Fri\b0\par\par\uc2 1,264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 11:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0914 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end +0.2% at fresh record high of 3618.478 in moderate volume, tracking gains in many Asian markets, with foreign buying dominating trade, traders say; expect shares to consolidate tomorrow ahead of weekend; tip range at 3600-3640. "Healthy foreign buying kept the main index in positive territory amid a generally cautious trend due to profit-taking by local institutional funds," says trader at Erdhika Securities. Foreigners net buyers of IDR244 billion worth of shares. Among gainers, gas distributor Gas Negara (PGAS.JK) +3.1% at IDR4,125, coal miner Adaro (ADRO.JK) +3.6% at IDR2,175, while Bank Negara (BBNI.JK) +1.9% at IDR4,075. Profit-taking hits \f28 \uc2 \f2 XL Axiata\f28 \uc2 \f2  (EXCL.JK) down 4.3% at IDR5,550. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0901 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/GBP's current pullback is clearly corrective says SEB, and once over the cross should head towards targets of 0.8886 and 0.8919. Now at 0.8780 the bank pegs support at 0.8774 and 0.8752. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0859 GMT [Dow Jones] After Wednesday's higher-than-expected September CPI for Poland, Nordea now expects a rate hike in the country to come at the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting on 27 October. "This will likely lead to some short-term positive momentum for the PLN after trading in a tight range of 3.90-4.00 for almost two months versus the euro." Nordea sees potential for a test of 3.83. It adjusts its EUR/PLN 3, and 12-month forecasts to 3.90, 3.80 and 3.80, from 4.10, 3.90 and 3.90 respectively. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0848 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD down late at 30.7700 vs 30.96.00 Wednesday, tracking regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' gains vs USD, but pair off fresh 26-month low of 30.540 on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , two traders say. Both tip \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought US$20 million late to support the pair. "Continued foreign inflows will continue to push up the local stocks and TWD," says one trader. Both tip pair may test 30.5000 support Friday. (lorraine.luk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0845 GMT [Dow Jones] Spot gold's rally could carry on until the FOMC meeting in November, as investors appear to be betting quantitative easing will pressure the dollar and other countries will try to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising sharply, says \uc2 Mitsubishi Corp\uc2  analyst Matthew Turner. "It's a rush into hard assets on the assumption that everyone wants a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and China doesn't want a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he says. Spot gold +0.8% at $1,382.75/oz. (matthew.walls@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0845 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys are lower in London trading as European equities mostly trade in the green and the EUR climbs to its highest level vs USD since January. Expectations of quantitative easing by the Fed continue to build ahead of a speech by Chairman Bernanke on Friday that could offer more clues on the Fed's thinking, although the rally in risky assets and a tick-up in inflation expectations have pulled Treasurys lower. Weekly jobless claims and PPI data are out at 1230 GMT, while the Treasury also auctions $13 Bln of 30-year notes. The 2-year note is down at 100-00+/32 to yield 0.365%, according to Tradeweb. The 10-year note is down at 101-22/32 to yield 2.43%. The 30-year bond is up at 101-03/32, yielding 3.812%. December bunds are down 0.04 at 131.53. December gilts are 0.05 higher at 125.26. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0840 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR forward premia higher as players think INR could weaken on fund repatriation once \uc2 Coal India\uc2 's IPO ends, says trader with foreign bank; 1-year forward premia at 2.36 vs 2.2975 late Wednesday. Few exporters willing to sell in market on growing view that spot INR strength may be temporary, may correct after funds targeting \uc2 Coal India Ltd\uc2 . IPO flow out if issue heavily oversubscribed, forcing rejection of initial down payment. Still, monthly WPI may support premia; data could renew expectations of interest rate hike at Nov. 2 policy meeting. Trader tips 1-year forward premia to target 2.4 in session.(bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0838 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP slides to 29-month low late Thursday, dragged by broad USD weakness against majors, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Pair at 43.16, lowest since May 2008 amid heavy trading. Pair may head toward 43.10 support, then 43.00 Friday, although traders expect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper PHP appreciation. "I'm sure these levels will be heavily guarded," says local bank trader; next resistance 43.30. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0830 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian government bonds higher as foreign investors continue to buy, though some analysts say yields don't look attractive anymore after recent sharp fall. "To me, the bond valuations are not attractive anymore, but that's not exactly slowing down capital inflows," bond analyst with state-owned bank says. 5-year yield down to 6.39% vs 6.42% yesterday; 10-year down to 7.02% vs 7.12%; 15-year down at 7.53% vs 7.59%; 20-year down at 7.86% vs 7.98%; and 30-year down at 8.26% vs 8.33%. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0827 GMT [Dow Jones] It looks like Europe is taking a little bit of profit on USD shorts with all the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs slipping a little against the greenback. EUR/USD trades at 1.4082 from its fresh 8-month high of 1.4123, USD/CHF climbs off a fresh all-time low of 0.9463 to trade at 0.9492 and AUD/USD just misses parity, topping out at 0.9996 and now trading at 0.9966. USD/JPY now trades at 81.15 from a fresh 15-year low of 81.03 and the USD index nudges up to 76.403 from 76.259, its lowest since mid December 2009. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0826 GMT [Dow Jones] The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was able to widen its parameters for allowable ruble fluctuations starting Wednesday because the main drivers for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been relatively subdued, but if volatile oil prices were to return, it might have to meddle in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than its current plan suggests, \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2  says. "In the event of higher oil price volatility, it will be hard for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Alfa economist Natalia Orlova says. Ruble strengthens to 35.4180 to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-euro basket, from 35.4798 late yesterday. Ruble strengthens to 29.9236 vs the dollar. (william.mauldin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0825 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR rock steady at 8,920 on suspected Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent local unit from appreciating further, dealers say. Four dealers say they suspect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought between $300 million-$400 million in total at 8,920 as foreign fund inflows continue. Pair likely to continue trading between 8,920-8,930 Friday with traders expecting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue defend greenback. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com) [ 10-14-10 0514ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101014e6ae0007e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
