\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Foreign Funds Pour Into Bank Indonesia Notes Despite Curbs\b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2010\par 10:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background)\par \par \uc2 By I Made Sentana\par \par \uc2 Of Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Foreign investors last month raised their investment in notes issued by the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in another sign that funds are continuing to pour into the country despite measures aimed at curbing short-term capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Like other countries in the region such as South Korea and Thailand, Indonesia has in recent months attracted a flood of foreign funds, pushing up the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to new highs against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners owned IDR64.7 trillion ($7.25 billion) of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes as of Sept. 30, up from IDR55.0 trillion as of Aug. 30, Bank Indonesia said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 This means around 26% of its outstanding money market securities was held by non-residents.\par \par \uc2 Foreign ownership of the securities peaked at IDR83 trillion in April before investors trimmed their holdings in the wake of renewed concerns over euro-zone debt problems to IDR36.4 trillion in May.\par \par \uc2 But foreign ownership has rebounded, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June introducing several measures to discourage short-term capital inflows, including the implementation of a minimal one-month holding period for the securities, and the introduction of paper with longer maturities.\par \par \uc2 This increase is part of a wider trend that has seen offshore investors similarly raising their holdings in the government's rupiah-denominated bonds to IDR186.76 trillion as of Tuesday from IDR182.26 trillion as of Sept. 30.\par \par \uc2 The influx of capital in search of higher yield has lifted the rupiah by around 5% against the dollar so far this year, to its highest level in 39 months.\par \par \uc2 The appreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made the country's exporters less competitive, a problem also faced by its regional peers, and traders said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on occasions to support the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com [ 07-10-10 0837GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101007e6a7000rc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
