\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Steady; 8,910-8,930 Tipped Friday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2010\par 11:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0935 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR steady at 8,920 as Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspected of continuing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow pair's slide. Dealers estimate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely to have bought nearly $300 million at 8,920 to slow pair's slide; creating narrow trading band of 8,918-8,926. Pair remains biased down as foreigners continue buying local stocks, bonds. Dealer says Bank Indonesia suspected of entering market since early morning, views as signal it wants pair to stick to 8,920; tips 8,910-8,930 range Friday. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0930 GMT [Dow Jones] Thursday's French auction received strong demand on cheap valuations, says Annalisa Piazza, Newedge strategist. Demand was strong across all three of the bonds on offer; OAT October 2020, OAT April 2026 and OAT April 2029. The new 10-year bond was covered 1.8 times despite the large size on offer. The 15-year bond was covered 1.75 times, following a good concession ahead of the auction while the OAT 2029 was covered 2.8 times, helped by a relatively small size on offer. "French debt offers good yields pick-up versus bunds and it might have supported investors demand," she says. (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0929 GMT [Dow Jones] The French debt offers good yield pick-up versus bund and it might have supported investors' demand at Thursday's auction of three OAT lines, including the new Oct 2020 OAT, says Newedge Strategy's economist Annalisa Piazza. France sold EUR8.490Bln of OATs versus a target range of EUR7.5Bln to EUR8.5Bln. She qualifies demand for the OATs as solid. Separately, \uc2 Commerzbank AG\uc2 's strategist David Schnautz says that after this supply being off the table, "we see a chance for some tactical recovery in 10-year OATs both on its own curve and in the core segment of the AAA-rated segment of the euro zone government bond market." (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds barely changed in lackluster trade. Yields dip in early trade, tracking overnight rises in U.S. Treasurys while continued fund inflows still bolster sentiment; but already low yield levels limit upside for price gains, says local dealer. Adds, if capital inflows not large enough, yields likely to hover around current levels amid normally quiet Friday trade. Eyes on Finance Minister, \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 's governor talk over baht appreciation. Minister hopes to come back from World Bank meeting in Washington with plan to deal with baht strength next week. Bid/offer yields of issue due December 2015 quoted at 2.45%/2.40% vs 2.45%/2.41% late yesterday, November 2016 at 2.62%/2.57% vs 2.62%/2.58%, June 2019 at 2.74%/2.70% vs 2.76%/2.73%. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0922 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia shares end higher after trading in tight 6-point range all day; market broadly negative with profit-taking dragging many large-caps lower after yesterday's rally; KLCI ends +0.1% at 1,481.45; dealer says market participants wary of taking large positions in absence of concrete directional cues, with most waiting for U.S. payroll data Friday after Wednesday's weaker-than-expected private-sector jobs data. Adds, on local front, investors will watch trade data due Friday, 2011 budget due Oct. 15. Market trend view remains positive; Maybank tips index to move into higher territory, but adds profit-taking may cap any rise; tips resistance at 1,483, support at 1,477. Decliners outnumbered advancers 410 to 299; glove makers continue slide after disappointing results yesterday from Top Glove (7113.KU), which down 3.3% at MYR5.50, Supermax (7106.KU) down 2.1% at MYR4.17. \uc2 MMC Corp\uc2 . (2194.KU) down 1.9% at MYR3.07. Among gainers, BAT (Malaysia) (4162.KU) +5.1% at MYR49.94, rebounding from losses over last couple of sessions after tax hike; \uc2 Malaysian Resources\uc2  (1651.KU) +3% at MYR2.09, AirAsia (5099.KU) +2.8% at MYR2.20. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0918 GMT [Dow Jones] With USD/CAD breaching trendline support at 1.02 the downtrend has resumed and a test and break of parity is next, followed by a retest of the 2010 low at 0.9930 says \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . Now at 1.0101 bearish pressure will remain intact in the absence of a daily close above 1.0160. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end down 0.5% at 3586.186 in moderate volume, off intraday low of 3540.779, as local funds taking profits in most blue chips after recent sharp gains, says trader; expect shares to continue to consolidate tomorrow; tip index in 3540-3600 range. "Healthy buying by foreign funds lifted the main index from its low," says trader at \uc2 Kresna Securities\uc2 . Foreigners net buyers of IDR224 billion worth of local shares. Among decliners: heavyweight Telkom (TLKM.JK) down 3.2% at IDR9,250, rebounding from IDR9,100-low, food producer \uc2 Indofood\uc2  (INDF.JK) down 5.3% at IDR5,350, off IDR5,200-low, while car maker Astra (ASII.JK) down 0.9% at IDR58,500, off IDR57,500 low. Bucking trend, \uc2 Indofood CBP\uc2  (ICBP.JK) up 10% at IDR5,950 on trade debut. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0912 GMT [Dow Jones] Yield spreads between European sovereign bonds remain relatively stable Thursday after successful French and Spanish auctions, with a slight tightening bias of the peripherals. The French Treasury sold EUR5.075Bln OAT October 2020 at an average yield of 2.68%, EUR2.29Bln OAT April 2026 at an average yield of 3.07% and EUR1.125Bln OAT April 2029 at an average yield of 3.15%. Spain sold EUR3.217Bln SPGB October 2013 at a maximum yield of 2.55%. The 10-year French German yield spread is unchanged on the day at 36bps, Spanish/German is 2bps tighter at 175.5bps, Italian/German is 1.5bps tighter at 151.5bps, Portuguese/German is 1bp tighter at 397.5bps, Irish/German is 3bps tighter at 421bps and Greek/German is 2bps tighter at 762.5bps. (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0912 GMT [Dow Jones] As Sensex zooms northward, foreign and domestic shareholders taking diametrically opposite positions: former on investing spree, latter selling off like nobody's business. Sensex +18.4% from June-September, driven mainly by foreign institutional funds, which have pumped $13.76 billion into Indian equities, according to Securities & Exchange Board website; local funds sold $3.56 billion worth in same period. Sanjiv Shah, executive director of \uc2 Benchmark Mutual Fund\uc2 , tips India as "attractive" choice for foreign funds mainly due to economic growth prospects; but local investors are trying to cash in gains from Sensex's appreciation, said Shah. "Some investors are driven by the fear component since Sensex saw a fall in January 2008 after reaching the same levels." But Nomura says in report there may be more steam before Sensex starts to correct. "Rising cash with domestic investors and continued foreign inflows is in sharp relief and could take the markets up further before a correction," it said. See: =WSJ BLOG/India Real Time: As Sensex Zooms, Foreign, Local Funds Diverge (suhita.poddar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0912 GMT [Dow Jones] Estonian consumer prices were up 4% from a year earlier in September, data released Thursday showed, and average inflation will be near 3% year-on-year in 2010, says Nordea bank. "The main culprit is expected to be food and energy prices, but also the recovering domestic economy will play its part in creating inflationary pressure," the bank adds. (charles.duxbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0900 GMT [Dow Jones] Safe-haven bunds drift lower as Spain gets good demand at an auction of 3-year bonds. Spain sells EUR3.217Bln of October 2013 bonds, with the bid-to-cover ratio rising to 2.16 vs 1.89 at the last sale. The average yield, however rises to 2.527% vs 2.276% at the last auction. December bunds are down 0.34 at 131.68. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0854 GMT [Dow Jones] Foreigners up investment in Bank Indonesia notes, in another sign funds continuing to pour into the country despite measures introduced in June aimed at curbing short-term capital inflows. Foreigners own IDR64.7 trillion ($7.25 billion) of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's SBI notes as of September 30, up from IDR55.0 trillion as of August 30, Bank Indonesia says; Like other countries in the region such as South Korea, Thailand, Indonesia has in recent months attracted a flood of foreign funds, pushing up value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to new highs vs USD. Though Bank Indonesia has said no plan to introduce further measures to curb fund inflows, analysts don't rule it out. (I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com) [ 10-07-10 0535ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101007e6a70006p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
