\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Lower; 8,900-8,930 Tipped Friday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2010\par 12:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1020 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR falls to 39-month low as foreign funds continue to flow into local debt, stock markets, dealers say. Pair last at 8,920 vs 8,910 earlier, 8,935 late yesterday. "The pair is heavily biased down, and it could have hit 8,900 if the Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  didn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," dealer says. Adds, BI may have bought around $200 million to stem IDR's rise. 8,900-8,930 range tipped for Friday. "Near-term, KRW, PHP, IDR and THB may continue to perform well on capital inflows and external balances," says Standard Chartered.(andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1020 GMT [Dow Jones] December bunds are down 0.05 at 131.76 and Nick Holt, a trader at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  cautions that momentum is showing signs of running out of steam. "If we cannot break back into the up-channel and close above 132.14, then a retrace will be on the horizon," he says. Support is at 131.53, 131.46, and 131.32. Resistance is at 132.00, 132.20, and 132.50. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1018 GMT [Dow Jones] The Irish government has repeated its reassurances to Anglo Irish senior bondholders Thursday, but \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  "can not help thinking that Anglo's senior debt should be subjected to a haircut too." Argues that the benefits to the sovereign ("by putting a stop to the money drain") would indirectly support \uc2 Bank of Ireland\uc2  and Allied Irish spreads, outweighing concerns that they too might be subject to a haircut at some stage. CDS written on Anglo Irish's senior debt were 25 bps tighter Thursday at 860 bps, while sub CDS were at 51 points upfront, 7 points higher, according to Markit. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1004 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex +0.8% at 20,107.60 as investors cover short positions ahead of close of derivate expiry for September. "Volumes have picked up sharply in banks and metal shares. These are the real contributors to the benchmark index's rise," says local dealer; adds, "funds are continuing to look for good investments at lower levels and this is one main reason for the short covering." Among gainers, HDFC (500010.BY) +3.3% at INR729.30, ITC (500875.BY) +2.7% at INR178.40, \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2  (500112.BY) +2.0% at INR3,256, \uc2 Sterlite Industries\uc2  +3.2% at INR166.60. Sensex tipped in 19,800-20,200 range Friday. (raghavendra.upadhyaya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1002 GMT [Dow Jones] South Africa's PPI reading for August was a touch higher than consensus expectations, but with little pass-through into CPI this isn't likely to trigger meaningful reaction, says Standard Chartered's Razia Khan. He adds: "It is a small point in favor of rates staying on hold, but PPI was never going to be the make or break factor." Annual PPI was up 7.8% after a rise of 7.7% in July. (robb.stewart@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0955 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end +0.6% at fresh 14-year high of 975.30 as capital inflows continue to cheer market sentiment. Strong August economic indicators including private investment, private consumption released earlier today also lend support. Big cap energy plays lead gains. "The SET index is likely to go up further on the back of capital inflows, but its pace would be slowed as profit-taking may emerge while it is approaching the 1,000-mark level," says Capital Nomura Securities strategist Chai Jirasevenupraphund. Notes, Thai shares so far chalked up 22.3% from closing level at end-June. Resistance at 977-980 zone, support at 963-965. Among most active, PTT (PTT.TH) +1.4% at THB297, Banpu (BANPU.TH) +0.9% at THB716, \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) off 0.5% at THB103.50, PTT Aromatics & Refining (PTTAR.TH) flat at THB27.50, \uc2 PTT Exploration & Production\uc2  (PTTEP.TH) +1.3% at THB154. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0949 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely to manage ample market liquidity until 1H 2011 via open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  (eg. hiking rates on NCDs, CDs) rather than hiking policy interest rates, says \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  economist Grace Ng. "The growing likelihood that the Fed will introduce further quantitative easing would increasingly raise concerns amongst EM policymakers, including the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , about capital inflow and impact on domestic liquidity going ahead." Adds, Taiwan's 12.5-bp hike today highlights island's solid economic recovery, gradual upturn of CPI. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0949 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/THB drops to 30.37 vs 30.47 late yesterday, tracking general bearish USD tone. Persistent portfolio inflows into local stocks, bonds keep bolstering THB while release of strong August economic indicators also THB supportive. Pair off 30.365 session low, also fresh 13-year low, on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say two dealers. "Most players are after the baht as all factors are pointing toward a firmer baht. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have bought several hundred million dollars, just like yesterday," says Bangkok-based dealer. Next support at 30.30 then 30.20, subject to broad USD trend over the weekend, resistance at 30.40. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0945 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CHF just made a fresh 30 month low of 0.9730 and \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  says there's more downside to come. The bank originally had a target of 0.9640, the 2008 low. However given the downside break of a 2-year contracting range and general USD weakness the bank says it cannot rule out a slide to 0.9325 in the 4Q. USD/CHF now at 0.9741. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0939 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar is sinking fast across the board, and its pattern against the yen is no exception. Having dropped to yet another post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  low of Y83.16 in earlier European trading, it's still hovering at Y83.30. If the Bank of Japan doesn't step in again soon, in line with its policy of continued vigilance on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it could get messy. "It's playing with fire," says Paul Mackel, an analyst at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 . If it doesn't come in soon, the market could pile in, he adds. (katie.martin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0937 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds slip into the red as demand falls at ECB's 6-day refinancing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Banks borrowed EUR29.443 billion at the facility, after a take-up of EUR104 billion at the 3-month cash tender Wednesday. With banks repaying EUR225 billion Thursday, lower demand brings down the excess liquidity in the system, while easing concerns about the banking system somewhat. December bunds are down 0.10 at 131.71. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0935 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CZK trades steady at 24.588-24.608 from 24.59 late Wednesday, remaining rangebound, shrugging of euro zone news of \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgrade of Spain, as it had largely been expected, a trader says. "EUR/CZK is only slightly moving above and below 24.6, but if the various indicators from global markets today bring some momentum to markets, we could see EUR/CZK move lower because the koruna is just looking for an impulse to return to stronger levels," the trader adds. (sean.carney@dowjones.com) [ 09-30-10 0620ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100930e69u00072\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
