Says this will be a "big challenge" for central banks in Asia, including Bank Negara. Bank Negara kept rates steady at 2.75% at its Sep. 2 meeting; bank to meet once before end of this year on Nov. 12. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0558 GMT [Dow Jones] Korea treasury bonds, bond futures sharply higher, tracking robust gains in 10-year bonds; Seoul-based traders say there's market talk some Asian investors collected large amount of 10-year bonds. Still, further gains unlikely as investors stay cautious ahead of industrial production data tomorrow, inflation data Friday, says IBK Securities analyst Ough Chang-sub. Expects profit-taking near term as yields very low. December bond futures last up 16 ticks at 112.53, 3-year quoted at 3.34% vs 3.37% earlier, 5-year at 3.75% vs 3.80% earlier. 10-year papers at 4.135% vs 4.20% last close. (kanga.kong@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0550 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei 225 December futures up 0.8% at 9570 on positive China PMI data for September and better-than-expected BOJ quarterly tankan business sentiment survey results. Investrust CEO Hiroyuki Fukunaga says (going further back in time), futures' recent rise mostly based on expectations for additional monetary easing by U.S. Fed and BOJ. "If economic conditions do not improve after the (anticipated) monetary easing is carried out, we may see a backlash, so it's hard to imagine futures going straight up from here," he says. Puts near-term index target at 9650 and end-October target at 9810. (kana.inagaki@dowjones.com) [ 09-29-10 0250ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100929e69t0004d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
