\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia - Market Factors to watch - Sept 16\b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 02:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds press digest)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Following is a list of events in Indonesia as well as news stories and press reports which may influence financial markets.\par \par \uc2 (Reuters welcomes your feedback, and for any queries please contact Sara Webb in Jakarta editorial on +6221 384 6364 or via email at sara.webb@thomsonreuters.com or on Reuters messaging sara.webb.reuters.com@reuters.net)\par \par \uc2 PRESS DIGEST\par \par \uc2 - BUMI RESOURCES MINERAL READY FOR IPO\par \par \uc2 PT Bumi Resources\uc2  Mineral, a unit of coal miner \uc2 PT Bumi Resources\uc2  , is now eligible to launch an initial public offering (IPO) as the company's assets are revenue-producing, said Eddy Sugito, a director of Indonesia's Stock Exchange. The company plans to float 20 percent of its shares, and expects to raise $200 million to $300 million. (Kontan)\par \par \uc2 - PAKUWON JATI TO REDEEM DEBT DUE THIS YEAR\par \par \uc2 Property firm PT \uc2 Pakuwon Jati\uc2  will soon repay all remaining debts of $3.64 million due in 2010, using internal cash, said Minarto Basuki, the company's finance director. (Kontan)\par \par \uc2 - SYAILENDRA CAPITAL TO ISSUE 3 MUTUAL FUND PRODUCTS\par \par \uc2 PT Syailendra Capital plans to issue three mutual fund products in October and aims to raise 350 billion rupiah ($38.95 million), said Anastasia Pritasari Ilham, head of marketing. (Bisnis Indonesia)\par \par \uc2 - LIPPO KARAWACI TO SELL SILOAM HOSPITAL TO FIRST REIT\par \par \uc2 Property firm \uc2 PT Lippo Karawaci\uc2  is ready to make an agreement on the sale and lease back of assets of Siloam Hospitals \uc2 Lippo Cikarang\uc2  with Singapore-based First Real estate Investment Trust (First REIT), said Ketut Budi Wijaya, \uc2 Lippo Karawaci\uc2 's president director, and will use proceeds to build a new hospital and maximise shareholder returns. (Investor Daily)\par \par \uc2 MARKET SNAPSHOT\par \par \uc2 * Asian stocks will probably rise on Thursday, helped by gains in the U.S. and a steadily falling yen <JPY=> in the wake of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [STOCKS-NEWS-ASIA]\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stock index <.JKSE> rose 4 percent to an all-time high on Wednesday and it was closed at 3.9 percent higher after a week closing for Eid al-Fitr holiday with \uc2 Malindo Feedmill\uc2  leading gains, up 23.48 percent, and Indomobil Sukses leading losses, down 19.61 percent. Bumi Resources led market turnover, rising 6.4 percent, and \uc2 Energi Mega Persada\uc2  had the top volume, steady from the opening at the market.\par \par \uc2 For prices see <0#.JKSE>, for news see [IF-E].\par \par \uc2 * Wall Street advanced on Wednesday but remained hemmed in a recent trading range as disappointing economic data hindered the S&P 500 from breaking through a stubborn technical level. [.N]\par \par \uc2 * Oil prices fell a second consecutive day on Wednesday on expectations that a key Canada-U.S. crude pipeline will resume after a week-long interruption, although government data showing a drop in U.S. crude stocks limited losses. [O/R] * Malaysian crude palm oil futures hit one-week lows on Wednesday, after data showing a strong buildup in stocks prompted a sell-off. [POI/]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  MARKET PRICES ---------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT @ 2354\par GMT -------------\par                 INSTRUMENT    LAST       PCT CHG   NET CHG\par S&P 500             <.SPX>       1125.07      0.35%     3.970\par USD/JPY             <JPY=>       85.6        -0.16%    -0.140\par 10-YR US TSY YLD    <US10YT=RR>  2.7225          --     0.000\par SPOT GOLD           <XAU=>       1267         0.11%     1.350\par US CRUDE      