2% to PHP59.90 and \uc2 Bank of the Philippine Islands\uc2  (BPI.PH), up 0.7% to PHP47.60, ahead of rights offer where shares to be sold at discount of around 30%, while losers paced by Ayala Land (ALI.PH), down 0.3% to PHP14.50 and Philippine National Bank (PNB.PH), down 2.5% to PHP37.55. PCCI Securities Brokers says aside from declines in U.S. share prices on weak earnings and jobless claims data, most of trending and volume oscillators are turning bearish for the near-term. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0216 GMT [Dow Jones] Bank Indonesia suspected of buying around $50 million with USD/IDR at 8,950 via state banks as pair slides to lows not seen since June 2007, three dealers say. "The amount of dollars bought by Bank Indonesia was small as the market is a bit thin," dealer with foreign bank says; suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifts USD/IDR slightly to 8,955 from 8,950, but pair still lower than 8,975 late yesterday. Bank Indonesia deputy governor Hartadi Sarwono told Dow Jones yesterday \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue "cautious \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to smoothen \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuation. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0215 GMT [Dow Jones] China government bonds lower on Shanghai Securities News report that China's regulator will raise amount it allows insurers to invest in stock market to 25% of their assets, from 20% currently; report fuels concerns that insurers, one of key investors in local bond market, might cut debt holdings to lift equities investment, says Guotai Junan Securities; notes \uc2 China Everbright Bank\uc2 's upcoming IPO also adds pressure to money market liquidity. Shanghai Stock Exchange government bond index at 126.00 vs 126.06 last close, likely in 125.9-126.0 band rest of session. (ming.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0210 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares likely sli