\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:EUR Falls;EUR/USD May Hit 1.200, EUR/JPY 105.0 N/T\b0\par\par\uc2 1,565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2010\par 07:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0553 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR again starts falling on growing concerns that euro-zone's sovereign debt turmoil has started to undermine health of region's financial system, may extend declines to 1.2000 vs USD, 105.00 vs JPY in near term, says Masanobu Ishikawa, manager of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Ueda Harlow. Notes many players have become worried over whether euro-zone's faltering financial system could drag down real economy in area; "it's extremely difficult to expect when the euro will hit bottom. Players remain very eager to sell the euro as economic conditions in Europe may worsen down the road." EUR/USD now at 1.2285 vs session high of 1.2372; EUR/JPY at 110.45 vs 111.62. Some traders say Europe investors just entering market, starting to sell EUR. (tomoyuki.tachikawa@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0552 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW off 1,277.0 high on another round of suspected USD selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to 3-Seoul based traders; but pair still trading higher at 1,259.0 vs 1,214.5 late yesterday in Seoul on concerns over tensions between North, South Korea. "It's a crazy market that (I) haven't seen in a while," says local bank trader. Adds, pair still biased upward despite "the aggressive (dollar) selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." Traders decline to provide near term USD/KRW. Pair has traded in wide 1,224-1,277 range so far today. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0543 GMT 0000 GMT (Dow Jones) The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's decision to decline to offer Swiss franc repos in recent days suggests it is unwilling to accept lower franc money market rates, says \uc2 UBS\uc2 . "We attribute the latest decline in franc interest rates and negative rates on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  forward market to the excess liquidity in the local money market rather than anything else," says economist Reto Huenerwadel. "It's a fact, however, that over the last days the monetary conditions in Switzerland continued to loosen," he adds. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0543 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY NDFs offshore extend gains on USD general strength vs major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; 1-year USD/CNY NDFs at 6.7560/6.7619 vs 6.7170/6.7220 late yesterday. Still, upside limited on lingering hopes China may allow CNY appreciation vs USD this year, says Hong Kong-based trader at Asian bank. "My personal feeling is that the one-year NDFs will be very toppish around 6.7700," trader says. (joy.shaw@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0537 GMT [Dow Jones] For now, probably best to simply get out of way of rallying Aussie bond market, wait for another time to try a little profit-taking, says Stephen Nash, head of strategy for FIIG. Korean concerns helped lift bond prices today, with 3-years up 10 ticks at 95.32, and though those concerns could dissipate easily, risk-averse market sentiment won't. "We are in this period of assessing just how bad the European growth outlook will be. That's going to take some time and during this period, any bad news will be featured," says Nash. "Not to mention, in terms of the RBA, the case for tightening has simply gone away for the time being." (geoffrey.rogow@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0535 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares down 2.1% at 728.97 midday in active trade, taking cue from regional slide following concerns over health of euro zone. Rebound after recent steep fall may emerge intrasession but unlikely to be strong enough to reverse benchmark to positive close, says Phillip Securities' Assistant VP Teerada Chanyingyong. Adds political situation still on radar as end of protests still leave consequent problems. Support put at 724, resistance at 742. Among top actives, PTT (PTT.TH) down 2.5% at THB236, Banpu (BANPU.TH) down 4.1% at THB564, PTT Aromatics & Refining (PTTAR.TH) down 3.6% at THB26.50, PTT Chemical (PTTCH.TH) down 6.0% at THB90.50. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0529 GMT [Dow Jones] China's move to hike investments in Syria masks challenges it is facing operating there. State-owned \uc2 China Petrochemical Corp\uc2 . (0386.HK) has struggled to maintain output from 2 Syrian fields acquired in $2 billion takeover of Tanganyika Oil in 2008. Fields produce heavy oil that is expensive to produce, difficult to refine. \uc2 Royal Dutch Shell PLC\uc2  (RDSB) said in April it was struggling to keep output from its fields in Syria's Dier-Ez-Zor area above 100,000 bbl this year. Last week, Shell sold 35% stake in Syrian oil unit to \uc2 China National Petroleum Corp\uc2 . But there is broader logic to China's Syrian investments, especially boost to its influence in Middle East, key strategic area. See "=CHINA ENERGY WATCH: Syria's Appeal Holds Despite Output Fall" (david.winning@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0519 GMT [Dow Jones] Aluminum contango financing deals which allow speculators, market participants to make money by storing metals and profiting from difference between cash and futures price likely to persist, says Adrian Lismore, deputy head of commodities marketing at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 . "Some of these deals are now being rolled over," he says. Aluminum financing has kept estimated 75% of global aluminum inventories off the market, supporting prices since 2008 financial crisis. Some market participants fear price of aluminum could fall below cost of production if interest rates rise or market flips into backwardation for some reason, which could cause deals to unravel, pushing glut of supply into market. LME 3-month aluminum at $2,051/ton, down $33 with 621 lots traded so far. (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0519 GMT [Dow Jones] S&P/ASX 200 down 2.4% at 4288.8, hits 2-day low of 4282.8, albeit on moderate volume. Index remains under pressure as offshore falls worsen, with Asian markets down 2%-3%, S&P 500 futures down 1.6% and AUD/USD down 0.9%. Markets are reacting negatively to tightening credit conditions, due to the European financial crisis, with 3-month Libor's rise to 10-month high causing widespread concern. "The markets are clearly very worried about credit conditions," says Patersons senior private client adviser Peter Morgan. "Company valuations are very attractive but a credit crunch can be diabolical and the fear factor is massive at the moment." Morgan says margin calls will be back on the agenda tomorrow if the S&P/ASX 200 closes below 4300.0 and Wall Street has another bad night. (david.rogers1@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0514 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares down 2.8% midday at 2536.547 in moderate volume with blue chips leading losses amid renewed worries over Europe's debt problems; support at 2530 vs 2532.331 intraday low, traders say. "Sentiment is very weak and many investors are worried because they think the bearish trend will continue for the rest of the month," says trader at Lautandhana Securities. Among decliners: gas and oil company Medco (MEDC.JK) down 6.5% at IDR2,500, car maker Astra (ASII.JK) down 3.6% at IDR36,550, Coal miner Bumi (BUMI.JK) down 2.2% at IDR1,740. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0506 GMT [Dow Jones] IDR showing unusual resilience in face of latest risk scare, will likely outperform other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  thanks to solid outlook for local economy, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that should limit any downside. USD/IDR down 0.7% YTD even as USD has made small gains vs most other Asians, which have been hit by concerns about economic fallout from Europe's debt crisis. Many analysts forecast USD may drop well below IDR9,000 before December vs IDR9,350 last. This reflects stark improvement in Indonesia's status among foreign investors, who sold IDR furiously in previous crises. Country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves +39% over last 12 months; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been using that war chest to support IDR, including suspected $20 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. Another key to IDR's resilience is \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's low exposure to euro zone-bound trade, as global markets fret over possible loss of demand due to unfolding sovereign debt crisis there. See: "=\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ASIA: Indonesian Rupiah May Remain Solid Despite Risk Aversion." (david.roman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0504 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  keeps March 2011 forecast for 10-year bond yield unchanged at 8.25% (currently 7.37%) despite sharp fall in yields as "inflation continues to trend above estimates (10% WPI, 15% CPI) and bond issues are still sizeable." Says, easing yields imply 3%-7% upside risk (assuming no loss/gain) to FY11 earnings forecasts for government banks with \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2  (500112.BY), Bank of India (532149.BY) being most rate sensitive. Notes, easing yields may boost near-term (1QFY11) earnings for government banks. "However, the big positive would be if banks, particularly SBI, was to use these gains to raise their non-performing loan coverage." House maintains marketweight on Indian banking sector with \uc2 Axis Bank\uc2  (532215.BY), \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  (500180.BY), \uc2 Bank of Baroda\uc2  (532134.BY) , Union Bank (532477.BY) and \uc2 Punjab National Bank\uc2  (532461.BY) as preferred plays. (subhadip.sircar@dowjones.com) [ 05-25-10 0153ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100525e65p00048\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
