elow IDR9,000 before December vs IDR9,350 last. This reflects stark improvement in Indonesia's status among foreign investors, who sold IDR furiously in previous crises. Country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves +39% over last 12 months; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been using that war chest to support IDR, including suspected $20 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. Another key to IDR's resilience is \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's low exposure to euro zone-bound trade, as global markets fret over possible loss of demand due to unfolding sovereign debt crisis there. See: "=\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ASIA: Indonesian Rupiah May Remain Solid Despite Risk Aversion." (david.roman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0504 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  keeps March 2011 forecast for 10-year bond yield unchanged at 8.25% (currently 7.37%) despite sharp fall in yields as "inflation continues to trend above estimates (10% WPI, 15% CPI) and bond issues are still sizeable." Says, easing yields imply 3%-7% upside risk (assuming no loss/gain) to FY11 earnings forecasts for government banks with \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2  (500112.BY), Bank of India (532149.BY) being most rate sensitive. Notes, easing yields may boost near-term (1QFY11) earnings for government banks. "However, the big positive would be if banks, particularly SBI, was to use these gains to raise their non-performing loan coverage." House maintains marketweight on Indian banking sector with \uc2 Axis Bank\uc2  (532215.BY), \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  (500180.BY), \uc2 Bank of Baroda\uc2  (532134.BY) , Union Bank (532477.BY) and \uc2 Punjab National Bank\uc2  (532461.BY) as preferred plays. (subhadip.sircar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0453 GMT [Dow Jones] JGBs higher as intensifying European fiscal issues and tension in Korean Peninsula propel investors to move their assets to safe-haven bonds, sa