\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: S&P/ASX 200 Down 2.5% As Offshore Falls Worsen\b0\par\par\uc2 1,744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2010\par 07:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0519 GMT [Dow Jones] S&P/ASX 200 down 2.4% at 4288.8, hits 2-day low of 4282.8, albeit on moderate volume. Index remains under pressure as offshore falls worsen, with Asian markets down 2%-3%, S&P 500 futures down 1.6% and AUD/USD down 0.9%. Markets are reacting negatively to tightening credit conditions, due to the European financial crisis, with 3-month Libor's rise to 10-month high causing widespread concern. "The markets are clearly very worried about credit conditions," says Patersons senior private client adviser Peter Morgan. "Company valuations are very attractive but a credit crunch can be diabolical and the fear factor is massive at the moment." Morgan says margin calls will be back on the agenda tomorrow if the S&P/ASX 200 closes below 4300.0 and Wall Street has another bad night. (david.rogers1@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0514 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares down 2.8% midday at 2536.547 in moderate volume with blue chips leading losses amid renewed worries over Europe's debt problems; support at 2530 vs 2532.331 intraday low, traders say. "Sentiment is very weak and many investors are worried because they think the bearish trend will continue for the rest of the month," says trader at Lautandhana Securities. Among decliners: gas and oil company Medco (MEDC.JK) down 6.5% at IDR2,500, car maker Astra (ASII.JK) down 3.6% at IDR36,550, Coal miner Bumi (BUMI.JK) down 2.2% at IDR1,740. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0506 GMT [Dow Jones] IDR showing unusual resilience in face of latest risk scare, will likely outperform other Asian \b \highligh